attribution: Words and music by Liliʻuokalani (1838-1917), written in 1878 and published with an 1884 copyright; public domain. Melody and word underlay follow the original sheet music, where some two-syllable words (pali, nihi, hele, liko, uka) are printed under a single note; the chorus keeps her two English lines. The passing G# shows as out-of-key.
source_url: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aloha_oe_song_02.png
